I have x-wing which also requires expanded memory.  I currently use Qualitas
386MAX, but I was able to run x-wing using EMM386.EXE without a special boot
disk or DOS 6's multiple boot configurations option.   

You can create a boot disk by typing FORMAT A: /S

Whether you use a special boot disk or not, include a CONFIG.SYS file and
ensure that it includes at least  the following lines:

DEVICE=[path] HIMEM.SYS
DEVICE=[path] EMM386.EXE RAM 1024
DOS=HIGH,UMB

Insert the path where the files are located (e.g. c:\dos\).

DOS 6's HELP command has information on EMM386.EXE, CONFIG.SYS, AUTOEXEC.BAT,
FORMAT.COM, and configuring multiple boot configurations.


